---
description: Release, verification and regression-test rules
globs:
  - "tests/**"
  - "backend/tests/**"
  - "*.bat"
  - "package.json"
  - "package-lock.json"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Tests must assert behavior, not merely the presence of strings, when behavior can be exercised cheaply.
- Never delete a failing regression test just to make a release green; fix the underlying behavior or update the test only when the contract intentionally changed.
- Keep Windows batch scripts fail-fast and return non-zero on failure.
- `PREPARE_HADES.bat` is the Windows preparation/setup gate. Its native-runtime build may warn and fall back to Python by design, but every non-optional setup stage must fail closed.
- `VERIFY_HADES.bat` is the canonical full Windows release gate and delegates to `verify_hades.py`; do not report full release verification unless that gate actually passes.
- Neither PREPARE nor VERIFY may print success when one of its own required stages failed.
- Update release/status documentation after verified behavior changes.
